###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Inference throughput of the EquiformerV2 models on an Nvidia A100 with
# MPtrj samples at batch size 1 (Table G.4): eqV2-S (31.2M parameters)
# 9.7, eqV2-M (86.6M) 7.1, eqV2-L (153.8M) 4.5 samples per second; held
# in the encoding input (timed on MPtrj samples, not on the Matbench
# set). Training cost is not reported in the version read.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Introduces OMat24 and sAlex. The OMat24 size in the data-set registry is the sum of the six splits of Table 1 (118,164,115); its level of theory is entered from Sec. 4.2. The origin-paper stub of this paper is removed from origin-papers.csv.
# - Table 2's caption gives MAE and RMSE 'in units of eV/atom', but the values (18 to 33, 67 to 81) and the text ('an energy-above-hull MAE of 18 meV/atom') are in meV/atom; meV/atom is used.
# - eSEN is a new registry method (introduced by Fu et al. 2025, not in the corpus). The eqV2-M OAM model is the registry model eqV2-M, whose run is declared here (origin set to this paper).
# - The pretrained OMat24 and OC20 checkpoints are not encoded as separate runs; they are the base models of the fine-tuned runs in the encoding input. Fine-tuning settings for the OMP (OMat24 -> MPtrj) and OC20 -> MPtrj models are not listed in Table G.2 and are not encoded.
# - F1, DAF, precision, recall and the other classification scores, and the thermal-conductivity SRME, are not accuracy metrics of the schema.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/barrosoluque2024.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

